This data portion of the module is run by using GitHub Actions. Below is the process that runs the automation:

#Create a Python file (Used [https://github.com/WJLM308/OSRS-Wiki WJLM308's Python script that runs the file] to create [[User:Keplare/200m xp code|the Python code]]
#Create a list of requirements (a.k.a. libraries) inside a requirements.txt that is within the same directory as the main Python file
#Create an update schedule .yml file, essentially the instructions for GitHub to run the bot daily at 00:00 UTC
#Set up the bot password on the Wiki for both the Wiki and GitHub to talk to each other. For example, if a bot username is update200mxp, the full username would be Keplare@update200mxp, and the password is whatever the algorithm sets up.
#Go to GitHub's directory and set up the bot username and bot password settings (not in the Python file directory, but in the secret variables themselves)
#Go to GitHub's Actions tab and run the .yml file.

